13
01:00:51,818 --> 01:00:57,818
The Rover is a 2014 Australian dystopian Western drama film written and directed
by David Michôd and based on a story by Michôd and Joel Edgerton.

14
01:05:32,727 --> 01:05:38,727
It is a contemporary Western taking place in the Australian
outback, ten years after a global economic collapse.

15
01:10:13,636 --> 01:10:19,636
The film stars Guy Pearce and Robert Pattinson, and features Scoot McNairy,
David Field, Anthony Hayes, Gillian Jones, and Susan Prior.

16
01:14:54,545 --> 01:15:00,545
It premiered out of competition in the Midnight Screenings section
at the 2014 Cannes Film Festival on 18 May 2014.

17
01:19:35,454 --> 01:19:41,454
The film screened at the 2014 Sydney Film Festival on 7 June 2014, followed by
the theatrical release of film in Australia on 12 June 2014.

18
01:24:16,363 --> 01:24:22,363
It had a limited release on 13 June 2014 in New York City and Los Angeles
before expanding wide on 20 June 2014 in the United States.

19
01:28:57,272 --> 01:29:03,272
The film earned seven nominations at the 4th AACTA Awards: Best Direction, Best Lead Actor for Guy Pearce, Best Supporting Actor for Robert
Pattinson, Best Production Design, Best Original Music Score, Best Supporting Actress for Susan Prior, and Best Sound, winning the last two.

20
01:33:38,181 --> 01:33:44,181
The film explores themes of australia, small town,
sibling relationship, hostage, dystopia.

21
01:38:19,090 --> 01:38:25,090
The tone is emotional.
